A||N||2||KG||2.5 engines?||||5||
Z||000000||KG||11-18-2001||08:08 PM||||are the other 2.5l engines the same as the ones in the fiero's? I have an 84' 5sp.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-19-2001||12:43 AM||||Well, if it's an '84 5 spd., somebody put it in after the fact.  All '84's with manual trans. came with the 4 spd.<P>There are basically two different 2.5L inline fours.  The front wheel drive version (like Chevy Citation's, Pontiac 6000's, and Olds Ciera's, Fiero's) and the rear wheel drive version (S-10's and Camaro/Firebirds).  The major difference is the mounting location for the starter.  The older rwd versions have a better cyl. head.  They don't have huge vanes in the intake runners, allowing more airflow.  They will bolt right on with, no problem, on a fwd block.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jim Jimenez||11-19-2001||01:42 AM||||If you want a exact replacement, you will need a 2.5 ("R" vin code) from a GM "X" or "A" car built during the 1984/86 model year. A 2.5 "U" from a Grand AM or Calais is not the same!||||reg||1
